# UI Component and Theme Standards

## Tech Stack Requirements

### Core Technologies
- **Next.js 16** with React 19
- **shadcn/ui** (New York style) - Component library
- **Tailwind CSS v4** - Styling
- **Radix UI** - Accessible primitives
- **next-themes** - Theme management
- **Lucide React** - Icon library
- **class-variance-authority** - Component variants
- **tailwind-merge** - Class merging utility

### Component Configuration
- Style: `new-york`
- Base color: `neutral`
- CSS variables: enabled
- Icon library: `lucide-react`

## shadcn/ui Component Usage

### Import Patterns

Always import shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui`:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card"
import { Dialog, DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle } from "@/components/ui/dialog"

// ❌ Wrong - Don't import from node_modules or other paths
import { Button } from "@radix-ui/react-button"
```

### Component Structure

Follow the shadcn/ui component patterns:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct - Use compound components
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Title</CardTitle>
    <CardDescription>Description</CardDescription>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    Content here
  </CardContent>
</Card>

// ❌ Wrong - Don't create custom wrappers
<div className="card">
  <div className="card-header">...</div>
</div>
```

### Available Components

Use these shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui`:
- `Button` - All button interactions
- `Card`, `CardHeader`, `CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter` - Content containers
- `Dialog`, `DialogContent`, `DialogHeader`, `DialogTitle`, `DialogDescription`, `DialogFooter` - Modals
- `Input` - Text inputs
- `Textarea` - Multi-line text inputs
- `Label` - Form labels
- `Badge` - Status indicators
- `Tabs`, `TabsList`, `TabsTrigger`, `TabsContent` - Tab navigation
- `Select` - Dropdown selects
- `Checkbox` - Checkboxes
- `Switch` - Toggle switches
- `Table` - Data tables
- `Avatar` - User avatars
- `Progress` - Progress bars
- `Skeleton` - Loading states
- `ScrollArea` - Scrollable containers
- `Sheet` - Slide-out panels
- `DropdownMenu` - Context menus
- `Slider` - Range inputs
- `Chart` - Data visualization

### Component Variants

Use built-in variants instead of custom classes:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct - Use variant prop
<Button variant="outline">Cancel</Button>
<Button variant="destructive">Delete</Button>
<Button variant="ghost" size="sm">Action</Button>

// ❌ Wrong - Don't add custom variant classes
<Button className="outline-button">Cancel</Button>
```

## Theme Implementation

### CSS Variables

Always use CSS variables for colors. Never use hardcoded color values:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct - Use theme variables
<div className="bg-background text-foreground">
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground border border-border">
<Button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">

// ❌ Wrong - Don't use hardcoded colors
<div className="bg-white text-black">
<div className="bg-gray-100">
```

### Available Theme Variables

Use these CSS variables defined in `app/globals.css`:

**Background & Foreground:**
- `bg-background` / `text-foreground` - Main background and text
- `bg-card` / `text-card-foreground` - Card backgrounds
- `bg-popover` / `text-popover-foreground` - Popover backgrounds

**Semantic Colors:**
- `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground` - Primary actions
- `bg-secondary` / `text-secondary-foreground` - Secondary elements
- `bg-muted` / `text-muted-foreground` - Muted/subtle elements
- `bg-accent` / `text-accent-foreground` - Accent elements
- `bg-destructive` / `text-destructive-foreground` - Destructive actions

**Borders & Inputs:**
- `border-border` - Border color
- `bg-input` - Input background
- `ring-ring` - Focus ring color

**Charts:**
- `bg-chart-1` through `bg-chart-5` - Chart colors

**Sidebar:**
- `bg-sidebar` / `text-sidebar-foreground` - Sidebar colors
- `bg-sidebar-primary` / `text-sidebar-primary-foreground`
- `bg-sidebar-accent` / `text-sidebar-accent-foreground`
- `border-sidebar-border`

### Color System

The theme uses **oklch** color space for better color consistency:
- Colors are defined in `app/globals.css` using `oklch()` function
- Dark mode colors are defined in `.dark` selector
- Primary color in dark mode is TrevOS green: `#2bc016`

### Dark Mode Support

Always ensure components work in both light and dark modes:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct - Theme variables automatically adapt
<div className="bg-background text-foreground">
<div className="border border-border">

// ❌ Wrong - Don't use mode-specific classes
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
```

### Theme Provider

The `ThemeProvider` from `next-themes` is available but not required in the root layout currently. The theme is applied via the `.dark` class on the HTML element.

## Styling Guidelines

### Use `cn()` Utility

Always use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

// ✅ Correct
<div className={cn("base-classes", condition && "conditional-class", className)}>

// ❌ Wrong - Don't use template literals or manual concatenation
<div className={`base ${condition ? "conditional" : ""}`}>
```

### Component Data Attributes

shadcn/ui components use `data-slot` attributes. Don't remove or modify these:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct - Preserve data-slot attributes
<Card data-slot="card">
  <CardHeader data-slot="card-header">
```

### Spacing and Layout

Use Tailwind spacing utilities consistently:
- `space-y-{n}` for vertical spacing
- `gap-{n}` for flex/grid gaps
- `p-{n}` / `px-{n}` / `py-{n}` for padding
- `m-{n}` / `mx-{n}` / `my-{n}` for margins

### Responsive Design

Use Tailwind responsive prefixes:
- `sm:` - 640px and up
- `md:` - 768px and up
- `lg:` - 1024px and up
- `xl:` - 1280px and up

## Icons

### Use Lucide React

Always use icons from `lucide-react`:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
import { Plus, Search, Edit, Trash2 } from "lucide-react"

<Button>
  <Plus className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
  Add Item
</Button>

// ❌ Wrong - Don't use other icon libraries
import { FaPlus } from "react-icons/fa"
```

### Icon Sizing

Use consistent icon sizes:
- `h-4 w-4` - Small icons (default in buttons, badges)
- `h-5 w-5` - Medium icons
- `h-6 w-6` - Large icons

## Form Components

### Form Patterns

Use shadcn/ui form components with proper labels:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
<div className="space-y-2">
  <Label htmlFor="name">Name *</Label>
  <Input
    id="name"
    required
    value={name}
    onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)}
  />
</div>

// ❌ Wrong - Missing labels or improper structure
<Input value={name} onChange={(e) => setName(e.target.value)} />
```

## Component Composition

### Compound Components

Use shadcn/ui's compound component pattern:

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
  <DialogContent>
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>Title</DialogTitle>
      <DialogDescription>Description</DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
    <div>Content</div>
    <DialogFooter>
      <Button>Action</Button>
    </DialogFooter>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Rules Summary

1. **Always use shadcn/ui components** from `@/components/ui` - Don't create custom replacements
2. **Use theme CSS variables** - Never hardcode colors
3. **Support dark mode** - All components must work in both themes
4. **Use `cn()` utility** - For conditional class merging
5. **Use Lucide React icons** - Consistent icon library
6. **Follow component patterns** - Use compound components correctly
7. **Use semantic color variables** - `primary`, `secondary`, `muted`, `accent`, `destructive`
8. **Preserve data-slot attributes** - Don't remove component metadata
9. **Use Tailwind utilities** - For spacing, layout, and responsive design
10. **Import from correct paths** - Always use `@/components/ui` aliases

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

- ❌ Don't import components from `node_modules` directly
- ❌ Don't use hardcoded colors like `bg-white`, `text-black`
- ❌ Don't create custom component wrappers when shadcn/ui components exist
- ❌ Don't remove or modify `data-slot` attributes
- ❌ Don't use other icon libraries besides Lucide React
- ❌ Don't use mode-specific classes like `dark:bg-gray-900`
- ❌ Don't skip labels on form inputs
- ❌ Don't use template literals for conditional classes
